tus="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OSAWA HIDEHARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OSAWA, HIDEHARU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A planar light source comprising LEDs, which is constituted of a light source (11), a light guide (12) optically connected to the light source and adapted to guide the light from the light source to one face thereof, and a reflective film (13) arranged on the opposite face to the one face. The light guide (12) is made of a material containing a wavelength changing substance (14) such as a fluorescent substance or a luminous substance (15). The desired color light is produced by changing the wavelength of the light from the light source (11), and luminescence is emitted while the light source is off.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur une source lumineuse (11) plane comprenant des diodes électroluminescentes et à laquelle est raccordé un guide (12) optique adapté pour guider la lumière de la source à une de ses faces, et un film (13) réfléchissant disposé sur la face opposée. Le guide (12) optique est conçu dans un matériau comprenant une substance (14) faisant varier la longueur d'onde telle qu'une substance fluorescente ou une substance (15) lumineuse. La lumière couleur désirée est obtenue par variation de la longueur d'onde de la lumière provenant de la source (11), et la luminescence est émise lorsque la source lumineuse est éteinte.AU0000262</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its f